        "detectedVersion": "1.3.2-r0",
        "present": true,
        "vulnerableCodeAssessment": "Exact image contains Alpine zlib 1.3.2-r0 (fixed version 1.3.2-r1) and mapped libz.so.1.3.2 SHA-256 a1e2c03dcdedba98a06a00cadfb67a0e0b1cd93986860ec0c5ce66e789c44e57. A recursive scan of 237 ELF objects found gzprintf/gzvprintf definitions in libz but no direct imports in any of 87 PostgreSQL loadable .so files. Direct libz.so.1 consumers include postgres, libxml2, pgcrypto.so, libLLVM, PostgreSQL dump/backup/receive clients and apk/libapk. postgres imports dlopen/dlsym; pgcrypto.so has DT_NEEDED libz.so.1. Therefore import-only absence is insufficient: a handle-based dlsym path could search the extension dependency chain. No valid PG-ABI adapter or trigger call path was demonstrated."
      },
      "upstreamFix": {
        "fixedVersion": "1.3.2-r1 reported by scanner; current official PostgreSQL tag still uses r0 at the same digest",
        "upstreamFix": "zlib commit df84af25dc1942490e1d1c899a07619152a46148."
      },
