      "attackerControlledInput": "The current exact database role polyhunter is superuser and LANGUAGE C is untrusted. A caller able to submit arbitrary SQL could meet the privilege gate for C-function DDL, but no application-controlled SQL injection/arbitrary-SQL route was demonstrated. Targeted source search found only fixed Drizzle queries and schema constants; this bounded search does not prove whole-program absence. Provider/query bytes do not by themselves establish the required valid gzFile and call sequence.",
