      ],
      "reachability": "Expanded static coverage and one live process snapshot now include all 237 ELF objects, all 87 PostgreSQL loadable shared objects, 59 extension control files, all direct DT_NEEDED libz.so.1 consumers, dynamic symbol matches and current mapped libraries. pgcrypto.so is installed but not active; only plpgsql is active. postgres imports dlopen/dlsym. PostgreSQL 17.11 load_external_function() calls dlsym(handle, funcname); pgcrypto.so directly depends on libz.so.1; POSIX specifies that dlsym(handle, symbol) searches the handle object and automatically loaded dependencies. This makes indirect symbol lookup plausible, but it was not directly executed on musl and does not prove a valid ABI-compatible gzFile/stall/formatted-call sequence or attacker-controlled SQL path.",
      "networkExposure": "Project-scoped Compose network; PostgreSQL has no published host port. This limits ingress but does not establish absence of an in-process database function path.",
